 {"candidate_version":"source-preserving-format-display-v3-complete-action-syntax","source_id":"SRC_9a28b3487c35ef666787854c","original_answer_sha256":"133229721e6d74701bf6854c30d730d3a5c89a969d10df24679b84a70082e313","view_sha256":"133229721e6d74701bf6854c30d730d3a5c89a969d10df24679b84a70082e313","offset_convention":"Python Unicode code points; end exclusive; no normalization","rows":[{"text":"**Chosen Method:** FDISCO","original_unit_ids":["L0001"],"original_character_ranges":[[0,25]]},{"text":"**Chosen Labeling:** [GFP (内源) + Alexa Fluor, MAP2 + Alexa Fluor]","original_unit_ids":["L0002"],"original_character_ranges":[[26,91]]},{"text":"**Justification:** FDISCO is specifically optimized to preserve fluorescence (including weak endogenous signals and synthetic dyes) for long-term storage (over 6 months) by using low-temperature dehydration and pH-adjusted solvents. For a 3 mm thick brain block, FDISCO provides excellent transparency and slight tissue hardening, which is ideal for repeated handling and imaging. To address the weak endogenous signal and the need for dendritic/local circuit analysis, a dual-target immunolabeling strategy is chosen: amplifying the sparse endogenous GFP with an Alexa Fluor secondary antibody, and co-labeling MAP2 with a different Alexa Fluor to visualize the detailed dendritic skeleton and local neuronal structures.","original_unit_ids":["L0003"],"original_character_ranges":[[92,813]]},{"text":"**Protocol Steps:**","original_unit_ids":["L0004"],"original_character_ranges":[[814,833]]},{"text":"Permeabilization and Blocking","original_unit_ids":["L0005"],"original_character_ranges":[[834,863]]},{"text":"Wash the fixed tissue block with 1x PBS. (Temperature: RT, Time: 1 hour)","original_unit_ids":["L0006"],"original_character_ranges":[[864,936]]},{"text":"Incubation with permeabilization buffer (0.2% vol/vol Triton X-100, 20% vol/vol DMSO, 0.3 M glycine in PBS). (Temperature: 37 ℃, Time: 24 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0007"],"original_character_ranges":[[937,1081]]},{"text":"Incubation with blocking buffer (0.2% vol/vol Triton X-100, 10% vol/vol DMSO, 6% vol/vol donkey serum in PBS). (Temperature: 37 ℃, Time: 24 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0008"],"original_character_ranges":[[1082,1228]]},{"text":"2 Dual-Target Immunolabeling","original_unit_ids":["L0009"],"original_character_ranges":[[1229,1257]]},{"text":"Incubation with primary antibodies (anti-GFP and anti-MAP2) diluted in antibody buffer (0.2% vol/vol Tween-20, 10 mg/ml heparin, 5% vol/vol DMSO, 3% vol/vol donkey serum in PBS). (Temperature: 37 ℃, Time: 72 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0010"],"original_character_ranges":[[1258,1472]]},{"text":"Wash with washing buffer (0.2% vol/vol Tween-20, 10 mg/ml heparin in PBS), changing the buffer every 4-6 hours. (Temperature: RT, Time: 24 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0011"],"original_character_ranges":[[1473,1618]]},{"text":"Incubation with secondary antibodies (Alexa Fluor 488 and Alexa Fluor 647) diluted in antibody buffer (0.2% vol/vol Tween-20, 10 mg/ml heparin, 3% vol/vol donkey serum in PBS). (Temperature: 37 ℃, Time: 72 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0012"],"original_character_ranges":[[1619,1831]]},{"text":"Wash with washing buffer (0.2% vol/vol Tween-20, 10 mg/ml heparin in PBS), changing the buffer every 4-6 hours. (Temperature: RT, Time: 24 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0013"],"original_character_ranges":[[1832,1977]]},{"text":"3 Tissue Optical Clearing (FDISCO Dehydration)","original_unit_ids":["L0014"],"original_character_ranges":[[1978,2024]]},{"text":"Incubation with 50% (vol/vol) THF (tetrahydrofuran, pH adjusted to 9.0 with triethylamine) in distilled water. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 12 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0015"],"original_character_ranges":[[2025,2170]]},{"text":"Incubation with 70% (vol/vol) THF (pH adjusted to 9.0) in distilled water. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 12 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0016"],"original_character_ranges":[[2171,2280]]},{"text":"Incubation with 80% (vol/vol) THF (pH adjusted to 9.0) in distilled water. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 12 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0017"],"original_character_ranges":[[2281,2390]]},{"text":"Incubation with 100% (vol/vol) THF (pH adjusted to 9.0). (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 12 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0018"],"original_character_ranges":[[2391,2482]]},{"text":"Incubation with fresh 100% (vol/vol) THF (pH adjusted to 9.0). (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 12 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0019"],"original_character_ranges":[[2483,2580]]},{"text":"RI Matching","original_unit_ids":["L0020"],"original_character_ranges":[[2581,2592]]},{"text":"Incubation with 100% (vol/vol) DBE (dibenzyl ether, RI = 1.562). (Temperature: RT, Time: 12 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0021"],"original_character_ranges":[[2593,2691]]},{"text":"Long-term Storage and Pre-imaging Treatment","original_unit_ids":["L0022"],"original_character_ranges":[[2692,2735]]},{"text":"Store the cleared sample submerged in 100% (vol/vol) DBE in a dark, airtight glass vial to prevent oxidation and fluorescence quenching. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 6 months)","original_unit_ids":["L0023"],"original_character_ranges":[[2736,2907]]},{"text":"Before repeated imaging or supplementary analysis, equilibrate the sample in fresh 100% (vol/vol) DBE to eliminate any RI mismatch or micro-bubbles caused by long-term storage. (Temperature: RT, Time: 2 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0024"],"original_character_ranges":[[2908,3117]]}],"removed_structural_prefixes":[],"nonformat_content_and_order_exact":true}
 
